{
  "schema": "chronolog-dataset/0",
  "dataset": "back-to-the-future",
  "title": "Back to the Future",
  "notes": [
    "Three character frames carry the events that character experiences, so one clock-tower night is stapled onto all three at the same coordinate. That collision is the point of the dataset.",
    "Alternate 1985 occupies the same Gregorian coordinates as the 1985 it replaces. It is separated by a group frame, not by a second connectivity mechanism: fixtures/time-travel-taxonomy.chronolog.json owns the fork/terminator claim and this dataset does not restate it.",
    "Events the films date only by year carry a year-only coordinate. The model records no precision, so those read as January 1 midnight; the missing level is the whole claim.",
    "Times are given where the films state them and omitted otherwise. A day-precision coordinate is midnight, not an assertion about the hour.",
    "Every frame here declares basis frame:wall-time, group frames included. A frame with attachments and no basis resolves to no calendar family, and its attachments' `day` level is then read as a raw count of days from the epoch rather than as a date."
  ],
  "requires": ["frame:wall-time"],
